  "chain_ok": true,
  "message": "VAT is now 25% in the code, and the test suite passes (2 of 2).\n\nThe changes are in two files:\n\n- **`src/vat.js`**: the multiplier is now `1.25` instead of `1.2`, and the comment says 25%.\n- **`test/vat.test.js`**: the expected values are updated. `withVat(1000)` gives 1250, `withVat(999)` gives 1249, and `withVat(250)` gives 313.\n\nThe 250 case is the one to check. 250 × 1.25 is 312.5, and `Math.round` rounds halves up, so it returns 313. If your pricing rules round half-even or down, that case needs a different rule. I didn't add one, because the rounding policy isn't in the repo.\n\nI searched the repo and found no other references to the 20% rate, such as docs or a README. I haven't committed anything.",
